## 3. Declarative Infrastructure Kubernetes Manifests

Apply the following Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs) via your GitOps workflow (e.g., ArgoCD or Flux) to provision the LLM Mesh topology.

### Cluster 1 Deployment (`aks-westeu`)

Save this block as `aks-westeu-agents.yaml`. This sheet configures the unified Azure OpenAI backend mapping and sets up the primary frontend conversational router.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: agent-mesh
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: frontend
---
# Unified shared model routing definition via kgateway
apiVersion: kagent.dev/v1alpha2
kind: ModelConfig
metadata:
  name: global-azure-openai
  namespace: agent-mesh
spec:
  model: gpt-4o
  provider: AzureOpenAI
  azureOpenAI:
    endpoint: "

https://azure.com

"
    apiKeySecretRef:
      name: azure-openai-credentials
      key: api-key
---
# Primary Inbound Routing & Orchestration Agent
apiVersion: kagent.dev/v1alpha2
kind: Agent
metadata:
  name: primary-orchestrator
  namespace: agent-mesh
spec:
  modelConfigRef:
    name: global-azure-openai
  instructions: |
    You are the head routing agent for enterprise requests on AKS clusters. 
    If a user request requires low-level pod analysis, log tracking, or performance metrics, 
    immediately delegate the work to the 'data-extraction-agent' situated in the 
    remote cluster profile. Do not attempt to process cluster queries locally.
  # Explicit A2A discovery declarations across boundary lines
  delegationTargets:
    - agentName: data-extraction-agent
      clusterContext: aks-northeu
      namespace: ai-analytics
```

### Cluster 2 Deployment (`aks-northeu`)

Save this block as `aks-northeu-agents.yaml`. This targets the analytics-focused cluster, anchoring the localized data worker and configuring its underlying Model Context Protocol execution interface.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: ai-analytics
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: tool-ecosystem
---
# MCP System Tool Registration
apiVersion: kagent.dev/v1alpha2
kind: ToolServer
metadata:
  name: cluster-log-mcp-server
  namespace: tool-ecosystem
spec:
  protocol: mcp
  transport: http
  httpEndpoint: "http://cluster.local"
  description: "Exposes secure tool hooks to view live performance logs and container metrics across local microservices."
---
# Specialized System Extraction Worker Agent
apiVersion: kagent.dev/v1alpha2
kind: Agent
metadata:
  name: data-extraction-agent
  namespace: ai-analytics
spec:
  modelConfigRef:
    name: global-azure-openai
  instructions: |
    You are a sandboxed cloud infrastructure data expert. Utilize your attached MCP log tools 
    to retrieve execution metrics and cluster debugging data requested by orchestrators. 
    Summarize the raw telemetry findings cleanly before returning results back to the mesh gateway.
  tools:
    - toolServerRef:
        name: cluster-log-mcp-server
        namespace: tool-ecosystem
```

