## 4. Verification and Mesh Diagnostics

Once the declarative configurations have been applied to your AKS instances, run the following commands to confirm operational health and trace cross-boundary mesh requests.

### Check Agent Discovery Status
Verify that Kagent controllers have mapped and initialized the local Custom Resources:
```bash
# Execute within West Europe Cluster Context
kubectl get agents -n agent-mesh --context aks-westeu

# Execute within North Europe Cluster Context
kubectl get agents -n ai-analytics --context aks-northeu
```

### Trace Multi-Hop LLM Request Telemetry
Kagent automatically injects OpenTelemetry traces across distributed prompt contexts. You can query the centralized mesh tracking endpoint to extract structured payload routing logs:
```bash
kubectl run mesh-trace-check -n agent-mesh --context aks-westeu \
  --image=curlimages/curl:8.10.1 --rm -i --restart=Never -- \
  curl -s http://cluster.local
```

